WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680
Electrical burns are uniquely dangerous, because they often cause significant internal damage

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.720
that you simply cannot see from the outside.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.760
Even if the skin injury looks small, the electricity traveling through the body can lead to irregular

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.200
heart rhythms, seizures, or muscle damage.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.280
When you encounter an electrical emergency, your own safety must be the absolute top priority.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.480
Do not touch someone who is still in contact with the electrical source, as the current

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.240
can travel through them and injure you as well.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.040
Instead, your first move is to ensure the scene is safe and, if possible, turn off the

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.880
power source immediately.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.400
Once it is safe to approach, call 911 right away if you haven't already.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.080
Remember that electrical shocks can cause the heart to stop, so if the person has become

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.200
unresponsive and stopped breathing, be prepared to start CPR immediately.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.040
For visible burns on the skin, you can treat them by covering the area with a clean, dry

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.320
dressing.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.520
Because of the high risk for internal injuries, anyone who has suffered an electrical burn

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.040
must follow up with a medical professional for a full evaluation.

